The formula multiplies the number of gifts times the number
of total artifacts (no idea if it includes your Quest one).
As a result any number of artifacts gotten by other means
have any effect on the first gift.  Name both Sting and
Orcrist, no effect.  Lawfull dip, no effect.  Heck, killing
A's for Sunsword and Demonbane and archliches for Magicbane
while going for atheist contact, no effect on the first
gift.

Let's see if I have it right on how the first gift is
generated:

For classes that get a specific one, that's it.  Mojo,
MB and so on.

For classes that don't get a specific one, the first gift
is co-aligned and does not draw from the unaligned list.
So lawfulls might get Greyswandir, neutrals might get
Mjollnir, chaotics might get Strombringer.

Last, the gift must be species appropriate.  Elves won't
get orcish weapons (Grimtooth), orcs won't get elven
weapons (Stormbringer, Sting, Orcrist).

If I add these all together, a chaotic elf who isn't a
class that gets a specific gift ends up with Stromy
guaranteed if they have named both Sting and Orcrist.
This could be a character who starts as a non-wizard
chaotic elf.


